From 393e193f5f2a0b8a42653a70f98ce3c8873e0439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:21:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-132: the CSV table's right-click menu -- Excel's
 cell menu, each item with its key; Shift+F10 (0.132.0)

The table had no right-click menu: everything was a key to remember.
- media/csv.js: cut / copy / paste, insert N rows above / delete N rows, clear contents, select
  row / column, find / replace -- the same functions as the keys, each key shown beside it.
  A right click inside the block keeps it (also on a selected row's / column's header);
  outside it selects that cell. Shift+F10 / the menu key open it at the active cell;
  Up / Down / Enter / Esc in it; any other key closes it and works as usual. Read only = the
  items that would change the file are off. A right press no longer starts a drag selection.
- extension.js: readClip -- the menu's paste asks the extension for the clipboard (a webview
  cannot read it) and pastes it like Ctrl+V (a cut block still moves).
- media/csv.css: the menu in VS Code's menu colours, with solid fallbacks.
- tests: csv_driver (items, keys, clear = one edit, Esc, Shift+F10 + Down + Enter, paste, read
  only), csv_realinput (a REAL right click, real keys, a real click on clear contents), smoke
  (readClip); the fake keeps the clipboard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
